FACT ASaveHasElevenSectionsTheLastReservedAndEmpty
	BASIS attested
	DESC "a save has 11 sections indexed 0 to 10, the last one being the reserved, empty part the"
		+ "terminating separator produces"
	ATTESTED_BY "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas/save-file.schema.json::Array of 11"
		+ "sections (indexes 0 to 10)"
	ATTESTED_BY "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas/save-file.schema.json::Section 10 —"
		+ "Reserved"
	SOURCE "Extracted from the ruling on section counters, names settled in the review of pull"
		+ "request 47"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST47

FACT ASectionLineIsOneJsonEntry
	BASIS attested
	DESC "each line of a section is one JSON entry, lines being separated by a pipe"
	ATTESTED_BY "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/fixtures/baseline_valid.json::{\"id\":44,\"woIds\":\"79111656,58524136\",\"size\":20}|"
	ATTESTED_BY "packages/shared-save-processing/parseSaveSections.js::return JSON.parse(line);"
	SOURCE "Extracted from the ruling on the single save parser, pull request 47"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST47

FACT ThePlayerIdentifierIsTheOnlyInt64FieldBeyondDoubleRange
	BASIS attested
	DESC "the player identifier exceeds the exact integer range of a double, and it is the only"
		+ "such field in the six reference saves"
	ATTESTED_BY "packages/shared-save-processing/serializeSave.spec.js::When a save holding an"
		+ "int64 player identifier is read back"
	ATTESTED_BY "packages/shared-save-processing/int64Identifiers.js::RAW_INTEGER_FIELDS"
	SOURCE "Extracted from the ruling on int64 identifiers, delivered by pull request 49"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST49

FACT FloatFieldsCarryADotZeroSuffixInFlatRecords
	BASIS attested
	DESC "the float fields of a save carry a .0 suffix when their value is whole, and the records"
		+ "of the format are flat"
	ATTESTED_BY "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/fixtures/baseline_valid.json::\"playerGaugeToxic\":0.0"
	ATTESTED_BY "packages/shared-save-processing/serializeSave.spec.js::should preserve decimal"
		+ "notation for known float fields in world objects"
	SOURCE "Extracted from the ruling on float suffix emission, pull request 36"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST36

FACT APlayerIdentifierIsASteamAccountReusedAcrossGames
	DESC "a player identifier is a Steam account identifier, which the game reuses from one game to"
		+ "the next and which is unique neither across two saves nor, formally, within one"
	BASIS hypothesis
	UNTIL "a save whose player identifier names no Steam account, or two saves of the same account"
		+ "carrying different identifiers"
	SOURCE "Extracted from the ruling on player identity, decision of 2026-09-07, pull request 39"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST39

FACT AWorldObjectMayCarryALinkedObjectList
	DESC "a world object may carry woIds, the list of the world objects it holds"
	BASIS hypothesis
	UNTIL "a source shows that the contents of a world object are only ever reached through its"
		+ "linked inventory"
	RATIONALE "The property appears on none of the 190338 world object entries surveyed: either it"
		+ "exists and the sample does not meet it, or it does not exist and the contents go through"
		+ "the linked inventory. It stays declared as a precaution: under a schema closed to"
		+ "additional properties, omitting it would reject a save that the reference rewrite claims"
		+ "to handle. If refuted, the type, the reference remapping and the matching line of the"
		+ "identifier rule go together, not the schema alone"
	SOURCE "Found on 2026-09-10, left open in the review of pull request 48"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST48

FACT AnAnimalHungerLevelLiesBetweenMinus100And100
	DESC "the hunger level of an animal lies between -100 and 100"
	BASIS hypothesis
	ATTESTED_BY "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas/section3-world-objects.schema.json::ranging"
		+ "from -100 to 94.22"
	UNTIL "a legitimate save is rejected by the hunger bounds"
	RATIONALE "The field was observed on the entries of a single group identifier only, 345"
		+ "occurrences over 190338, ranging from -100 to 94.22. The symmetric scale rests on an"
		+ "animal yielding a DNA sequence when its level is positive, which is consistent with a"
		+ "ceiling without proving it. It is exactly the risk the schema rule names, a bound set on"
		+ "the sample alone rejecting a legitimate save; the user accepted that risk"
		REF @DECISION.ASchemaRuleHoldsByMeaningBeforeMeasurement
	SOURCE "Found on 2026-09-10 in pull request 48"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST48

FACT ProceduralWrecksAreSpawnedByThePortalGenerator
	DESC "the ProceduralWreck objects and ProceduralInstanceGenerator are spawned by"
		+ "PortalGenerator1, the portal generator"
	BASIS hypothesis
	UNTIL "a save or a game source shows procedural wrecks spawned without PortalGenerator1"
	RATIONALE "ProceduralInstanceGenerator has no label and renders its own key; once the link is"
		+ "established the label table would name it, names being attested by a source or a save."
		+ "The question was left as a code comment in worldObjectLabels, kept there and pointing at"
		+ "this entity"
		REF @DECISION.WorldObjectNamesAreAttestedBySourceOrSave
		REF @DECISION.ACodeCommentQuestionNamesItsCorpusEntity
	SOURCE "User ruling of 2026-09-14 in the review of pull request 76"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST76
